@class
    @name=BBCode
    @brief=The section describes BBCode that is used to format the source code
    @key=bbcode
    @ingroup=sources
    @type=tags
    @membersToContent=true

    The BBCode is well-know formatting specification actively used
    in phpbb forums and their descendants.

    BBCode is supported only by output templates that has the option
    to format the text. In order to have bbcode processed make sure
    that `default-transform` option is enabled in the output template.

    BBCode tags should be put in square brackets [c][][/c].

    The opening bbcode tag has format [b][[i]tagName[/i]][/b]

    The closing bbcode tag has format [b][[i]/tagName[/i]][/b]

    Typically, bbcode with a few exceptions are applied to the text between opening
    and closing bbcodes, e.g. [c]text [[nil]b]bold[[nil]/b] text[/c] will
    be displayed as 'text [b]bold[/b] text'. Exceptions are tags [c][[nil]nil][/c], [c][[nil]br][/c],
    [c][[nil]img][/c].

    There is no special character to escape an opening square bracket because if it is not
    recognized as a bbcode, the compiler simply adds it to the text. However, if
    there is the text that is a correct bbcode, but you want to display it as is, for example
    [c]myArray[[nil]i] + 1[/c] in C++ example will be displayed as
    '[c]myArray[i] + 1[/i][/c]. To make example look correctly, add [c][[nil]nil][/c] tag
    after opening square bracket 'breaking' the correct pattern: [c]myArray[[[nil]nil]i] + 1[/c],

    If bbcode has a value, the value is set after [c]=[/c] character after the bbcode name, for example:
    [c][[nil]color=red]red[[[nil]/color][/c].

    BBCodes may be used inside other bbcodes, for example:
    [c][[nil]b]myt[[nil]i]e[[nil]sub]xt[[nil]/sub] is [[nil]/i] heavi[[nil]/b]ly [[nil]u]for[[nil]color=gray]mat[[nil]/color]ted[[nil]/u][/c].
    ('[b]myt[i]e[sub]xt[/sub] is [/i] heavi[/b]ly [u]for[color=gray]mat[/color]ted[/u]').

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=b
        @brief=Make text bold
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=s
        @brief=Make text strikedthrough
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=i
        @brief=Make text italic
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=u
        @brief=Underline the text
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=c
        @brief=Make text code (monospace)
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=sup
        @brief=Make text superscript
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=sub
        @brief=Make text subscript
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=size=
        @brief=Increase or decrease the size of the text
        @custom=xml-tag

        @param
            @name=size
            Relative size of the text, use `+n` to increase the fond and `-n` to decrease the font, e.g.
            `[[nil]size=+1]slightly bigger[[nil]/size]`.
        @end
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=red
        @brief=Make text red
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=green
        @brief=Make text green
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=blue
        @brief=Make text blue
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=gray
        @brief=Make text dark gray
        @custom=xml-tag
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=color=
        @brief=Sets the color of the text
        @custom=xml-tag

        @param
            @name=color
            A name of the web-color to set or RBG color reference.
        @end
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=link=
        @brief=A link to another topic
        @custom=xml-tag
        @param
            @name=link
            A key of another topic.
        @end
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=clink
        @brief=A link to another topic displayed as a code
        @custom=xml-tag

        The tag `[[nil]clink=key]text[[nil]/clink]` gives exactly
        the same result as
        `[[nil]link=key][[nil]c]text[[nil]/c][[nil]/link]`.
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=url=
        @brief=A link to specified URL to be opened in the same window
        @custom=xml-tag

        @param
            @name=url
            http or https link to be opened.
        @end

    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=eurl
        @brief=A link to specified URL to be opened in a new window
        @custom=xml-tag

        @param
            @name=url
            http or https link to be opened.
        @end
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=img=
        @brief=Inserts an image
        @custom=xml-tag

        @param
            @name=img
            The relative or absolute URL to the image.
        @end

        Note: this tag has NO closing tag, e.g. `[[nil]img=myimage.png]`
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=br
        @brief=Inserts a page break.
        @custom=xml-tag

        Note: this tag has NO closing tag, e.g. `[[nil]br]`
    @end
    @member
        @type=property
        @name=nil
        @brief=Tag that displays nothing.
        @custom=xml-tag

        The tag is useful when you need to "break" default behavior of the parser, e.g.
        when you need to insert a bbcode as a part of the text.

        Example: `[[nil]b]text[[nil]/b]` will be displayed as [b]text[/b]

        Example: `[[[nil]nil]b]text[[[nil]nil]/b]` will be displayed as `[[nil]b]text[[nil]/b]`

        Note: this tag has NO closing tag.
    @end
@end
